   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 3. Part 2: Working with Alignment Files (pysam) <a name=\"pysam\"></a>\n",
    "\n",
    "Pysam is used to work with SAM/BAM files (sequence alignment files).\n",
    "\n",
    "### 3.1 Download Sample BAM File"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Download a small sample BAM file\n",
    "!wget -q https://github.com/pysam-developers/pysam/raw/master/tests/ex1.bam\n",
    "!wget -q https://github.com/pysam-developers/pysam/raw/master/tests/ex1.bam.bai\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✅ Downloaded sample BAM file (ex1.bam)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 3.2 Reading and Exploring BAM Files"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Open BAM file\n",
    "bamfile = pysam.AlignmentFile(\"ex1.bam\", \"rb\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Get basic statistics\n",
    "print(\"BAM File Statistics:\")\n",
    "print(f\"Number of references: {bamfile.nreferences}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Reference names: {bamfile.references}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Reference lengths: {bamfile.lengths}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Count total reads\n",
    "total_reads = bamfile.count()\n",
    "print(f\"\\nTotal reads: {total_reads}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Reset iterator\n",
    "bamfile.close()\n",
    "bamfile = pysam.AlignmentFile(\"ex1.bam\", \"rb\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Examine first few reads\n",
    "print(\"\\nFirst 5 aligned reads:\")\n",
    "print(\"-\" * 80)\n",
    "\n",
    "for i, read in enumerate(bamfile.fetch()):\n",
    "    if i >= 5:\n",
    "        break\n",
    "    print(f\"\\nRead {i+1}:\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  Query name: {read.query_name}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  Reference: {read.reference_name}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  Position: {read.reference_start}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  Mapping quality: {read.mapping_quality}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  Is paired: {read.is_paired}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  Is mapped: {not read.is_unmapped}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  Sequence length: {read.query_length}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "bamfile.close()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 3.3 Calculate Coverage Statistics"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Calculate per-position coverage for a specific region\n",
    "bamfile = pysam.AlignmentFile(\"ex1.bam\", \"rb\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Get coverage for first reference\n",
    "ref_name = bamfile.references[0]\n",
    "coverage = bamfile.count_coverage(ref_name, start=0, stop=100)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Sum coverage across all nucleotides\n",
    "total_coverage = [sum(x) for x in zip(*coverage)]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Coverage for {ref_name} (positions 0-100):\")\n",
    "print(f\"Mean coverage: {np.mean(total_coverage):.2f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Max coverage: {max(total_coverage)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Min coverage: {min(total_coverage)}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "bamfile.close()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 4. Part 3: Variant Analysis (PyVCF) <a name=\"pyvcf\"></a>\n",
    "\n",
    "VCF (Variant Call Format) files store information about genetic variants.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 4.1 Download Sample VCF File"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Download sample VCF file\n",
    "!wget -q https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jamescasbon/PyVCF/master/vcf/test/example-4.0.vcf -O sample.vcf\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✅ Downloaded sample VCF file\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 4.2 Reading and Parsing VCF Files"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Read VCF file\n",
    "vcf_reader = vcf.Reader(open('sample.vcf', 'r'))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"VCF File Information:\")\n",
    "print(f\"Samples: {vcf_reader.samples}\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\nMetadata:\")\n",
    "for key, value in vcf_reader.metadata.items():\n",
    "    print(f\"  {key}: {value}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Parse variants\n",
    "vcf_reader = vcf.Reader(open('sample.vcf', 'r'))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nFirst 5 variants:\")\n",
    "print(\"-\" * 100)\n",
    "\n",
    "variant_data = []\n",
    "for i, record in enumerate(vcf_reader):\n",
    "    if i >= 5:\n",
    "        break\n",
    "    \n",
    "    print(f\"\\nVariant {i+1}:\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  Chromosome: {record.CHROM}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  Position: {record.POS}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  ID: {record.ID}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  Reference: {record.REF}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  Alternate: {record.ALT}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  Quality: {record.QUAL}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  Filter: {record.FILTER}\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Store for later analysis\n",
    "    variant_data.append({\n",
    "        'CHROM': record.CHROM,\n",
    "        'POS': record.POS,\n",
    "        'REF': record.REF,\n",
    "        'ALT': str(record.ALT[0]) if record.ALT else None,\n",
    "        'QUAL': record.QUAL\n",
    "    })"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 4.3 Filter Variants by Quality"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Filter high-quality variants\n",
    "vcf_reader = vcf.Reader(open('sample.vcf', 'r'))\n",
    "\n",
    "high_quality_variants = []\n",
    "quality_threshold = 30\n",
    "\n",
    "for record in vcf_reader:\n",
    "    if record.QUAL and record.QUAL >= quality_threshold:\n",
    "        high_quality_variants.append(record)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Variants with quality >= {quality_threshold}: {len(high_quality_variants)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\nExample high-quality variant:\")\n",
    "if high_quality_variants:\n",
    "    var = high_quality_variants[0]\n",
    "    print(f\"  {var.CHROM}:{var.POS} {var.REF}>{var.ALT[0]} (Q={var.QUAL})\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 5. Part 4: Genomic Intervals (pybedtools) <a name=\"pybedtools\"></a>\n",
    "\n",
    "Pybedtools is a Python wrapper for BEDTools, used for genomic interval operations.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 5.1 Create BED Files"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create sample BED files\n",
    "bed_content_1 = \"\"\"chr1\\t100\\t200\\tfeature1\\t100\\t+\n",
    "chr1\\t300\\t400\\tfeature2\\t200\\t+\n",
    "chr1\\t500\\t600\\tfeature3\\t150\\t-\n",
    "chr2\\t100\\t250\\tfeature4\\t300\\t+\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "bed_content_2 = \"\"\"chr1\\t150\\t250\\tgene1\\t50\\t+\n",
    "chr1\\t350\\t450\\tgene2\\t75\\t+\n",
    "chr2\\t50\\t200\\tgene3\\t100\\t-\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "with open('features.bed', 'w') as f:\n",
    "    f.write(bed_content_1)\n",
    "\n",
    "with open('genes.bed', 'w') as f:\n",
    "    f.write(bed_content_2)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✅ Created BED files: features.bed and genes.bed\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 5.2 Basic BED Operations"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load BED files\n",
    "features = pybedtools.BedTool('features.bed')\n",
    "genes = pybedtools.BedTool('genes.bed')\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Features BED file:\")\n",
    "print(features)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nGenes BED file:\")\n",
    "print(genes)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 5.3 Find Overlapping Intervals"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Find intersections between features and genes\n",
    "intersections = features.intersect(genes, wa=True, wb=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Overlapping intervals:\")\n",
    "print(\"-\" * 80)\n",
    "for interval in intersections:\n",
    "    print(f\"Feature: {interval[0]}:{interval[1]}-{interval[2]} ({interval[3]})\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Overlaps with Gene: {interval[6]}:{interval[7]}-{interval[8]} ({interval[9]})\")\n",
    "    print()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Count overlaps\n",
    "overlap_count = len(intersections)\n",
    "print(f\"Total overlapping intervals: {overlap_count}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 5.4 Merge Intervals"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Merge overlapping intervals\n",
    "merged = features.merge()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Original features:\")\n",
    "for interval in features:\n",
    "    print(f\"  {interval[0]}:{interval[1]}-{interval[2]}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nMerged features:\")\n",
    "for interval in merged:\n",
    "    print(f\"  {interval[0]}:{interval[1]}-{interval[2]}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 6. Part 5: Scikit-bio for Sequence Analysis <a name=\"scikitbio\"></a>\n",
    "\n",
    "Scikit-bio provides additional bioinformatics algorithms and data structures.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 6.1 DNA Sequence Operations"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create DNA sequence using scikit-bio\n",
    "dna = DNA('ATGGCCATTGTAATGGGCCGCTGAAAGGGTGCCCGATAG')\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"DNA Sequence:\")\n",
    "print(dna)\n",
    "print(f\"Length: {len(dna)}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# GC content\n",
    "gc = dna.gc_content()\n",
    "print(f\"\\nGC content: {gc:.2%}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Complement and reverse complement\n",
    "print(\"\\nComplement:\")\n",
    "print(dna.complement())\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nReverse complement:\")\n",
    "print(dna.reverse_complement())\n",
    "\n",
    "# Transcribe to RNA\n",
